1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Demo: start the service, then ask questions from the terminal.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,133
Start the service with one command. It listens on port 8000 (set PORT to change it).

3
00:00:09,133 --> 00:00:14,133
Startup: the 10 policies are split into 48 sections and indexed (embeddings + BM25).

4
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:26,667
Check the service is up: GET /health

5
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:55,133
Ask a question (README example). The answer cites the document, section and an exact quote.

6
00:00:55,133 --> 00:01:23,600
A question that needs two policies: travel (hotel limit) and expenses (who approves).

7
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:52,600
Applying a rule to a situation: the gift is above the NGN 15,000 limit, so it must be declared.

8
00:01:52,600 --> 00:02:20,667
Two policies again: training repayment (learning policy) and leave payout (annual leave policy).

9
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:35,533
Not covered by any policy: the assistant refuses instead of guessing, with no citations.

10
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:49,867
Invalid input (empty question) returns HTTP 422 with an error body, not a fake refusal.

11
00:02:49,867 --> 00:02:55,867
Failures are reported honestly in results.csv and WRITEUP.md.
